### LeadLens API walkthrough
### Run the backend (cd backend && mvn spring-boot:run), then click "Send Request" on each block
### (VS Code REST Client / IntelliJ HTTP Client), or copy the curl equivalents from the README.

@base = http://localhost:8080

### 1. Load the bundled 36-row SaaSquatch-style export
POST {{base}}/api/imports/sample

### 2. Watch verification + enrichment finish (status RUNNING -> DONE)
GET {{base}}/api/imports/latest

### 3. Dashboard numbers: tiers, ready-to-contact, bad contacts caught, duplicates merged
GET {{base}}/api/stats

### 4. The ranked list: Tier A with a verified personal email
GET {{base}}/api/leads?tier=A&contact=verified&sort=score,desc

### 5. Ask in plain English -> filters (Claude with ANTHROPIC_API_KEY, rule parser without)
POST {{base}}/api/leads/ask
Content-Type: application/json

{ "question": "family-owned HVAC in Texas over 20 years, not contacted" }

### 6. Apply the filters the answer returned
GET {{base}}/api/leads?industry=HVAC&state=TX&minYears=20&signal=FAMILY_OWNED&status=NEW

### 7. One lead in full: score components, reasons, signals with evidence, next action
GET {{base}}/api/leads/1

### 8. Write the outreach brief (why now, talking points, first email, call opener)
POST {{base}}/api/leads/1/brief

### 9. Log a touch: the follow-up is scheduled 3 business days out
PATCH {{base}}/api/leads/1
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "CONTACTED" }

### 10. Today's call list: due follow-ups first, then the best untouched leads
GET {{base}}/api/leads/today?limit=10

### 11. Insights: funnel, best segments, data quality, recommendations
GET {{base}}/api/insights

### 12. Change the buy box: every lead is re-scored, the response shows the tier shift
PUT {{base}}/api/thesis
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "mode": "ACQUISITION",
  "industries": ["HVAC", "plumbing"],
  "locations": ["TX", "FL"],
  "minEmployees": 10, "maxEmployees": 100,
  "minRevenue": 2000000, "maxRevenue": 20000000,
  "minYearsInBusiness": 20,
  "excludeKeywords": ["franchise"]
}

### 13. Export the current view for HubSpot (CSV download)
GET {{base}}/api/leads/export?format=hubspot&tier=A,B

### 14. Configure a CRM webhook (Zapier / Make / n8n / HubSpot workflow) and push the view
PUT {{base}}/api/integrations/webhook
Content-Type: application/json

{ "url": "https://hooks.zapier.com/hooks/catch/123/abc" }

###
POST {{base}}/api/integrations/webhook/send?tier=A

### 15. Build leads from websites only (live crawl; obeys robots.txt)
POST {{base}}/api/imports/websites
Content-Type: application/json

{ "text": "basecamp.com\nwordpress.org" }
